hadiths[315]{hadithnumber,text}:
"475","[AI-translation] From Jarir who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, while he was receiving pledges, and I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Stretch forth your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you, and lay down conditions upon me, for you are more knowing."" He said: ""I take your pledge upon [the condition] that you worship Allah, establish the prayer, give the zakah, offer sincere advice to the Muslims, and separate from the idolaters."
"476","[AI-translation] Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, ascended the pulpit and said: ""No, I swear! No, I swear! No, I swear!"" Then he descended and said: ""Glad tidings, glad tidings! Whoever prays the five prayers and avoids the major sins will enter from whichever gate of Paradise he wishes."" Al-Muttalib said: I heard a man asking Abdullah ibn Amr, ""Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, mention them?"" He said: ""Yes: being undutiful to parents, associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, accusing chaste women, consuming the wealth of an orphan, fleeing from the battlefield, and consuming usury."
"477","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Amr who said: We prayed the Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. Some departed and some stayed behind. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came hurriedly, out of breath, with his garment drawn up above his knees, and said: ""Glad tidings! Your Lord has opened a door of the gates of the heavens to boast of you to the angels, saying: 'Look at My servants! They have fulfilled an obligatory prayer and are waiting for another.'"
"478","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Build it as an 'arish like the 'arish of Musa."" Meaning the mosque of Madinah. It is narrated mursalan from Al-Hasan al-Basri, Salim ibn Atiyyah, Al-Zuhri, and Rashid ibn Sa'd, and musndan from Abu al-Darda and Ubadah ibn al-Samit."
"479","On the authority of Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī, who said: I was in a gathering of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among whom was ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit. They mentioned the Witr prayer. Some of them said it was obligatory, and some said it was a Sunnah. ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit said: ""As for me, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Gabriel came to me from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and said: O Muḥammad, Allah the Mighty and Majestic said to you: I have made obligatory upon your Ummah five prayers. Whoever meets them with their ablutions, their times, and their prostrations, then he has a covenant with Me that I will admit him into Paradise through them. And whoever meets Me having diminished anything from that, or something resembling it, then he has no covenant with Me. If I will, I will punish him, and if I will, I will have mercy on him.'"""
"480","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Muadh ibn Jabal prayed Isha with his companions and made it long for them. So a man from among us left and prayed alone. Muadh was informed about him and said, ""He is a hypocrite."" When that reached the man, he entered upon the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and informed him of what Muadh had said. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Do you want to be a source of trial, O Muadh?! When you lead the people, recite: 'By the sun and its brightness,' 'Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High,' 'By the night when it envelops,' and 'Read in the name of your Lord.'"
"481","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, giving a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: ""Fear Allah, your Lord; pray your five [prayers]; fast your month; give the zakah of your wealth; and obey the one in authority over you, [and] you will enter the Paradise of your Lord."
"482","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, turned his face toward us when he stood for the prayer, before he pronounced the takbir, and said: ""Complete the rows (and in a narration: straighten up, straighten up) and stand close together, for I see you behind my back (just as I see you in front of me)."
"483","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, marfu'an: ""Two whose prayers do not go beyond their heads: a slave who has fled from his masters until he returns to them, and a woman who disobeys her husband until she returns."
"484","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Make between your adhan and iqamah a breathing space equal to the time it takes for one in need to fulfill his need with ease, and the time it takes the eater to finish his food in leisure."" It is reported from the hadith of Ubayy ibn Kab, Jabir ibn Abdullah, Abu Hurayrah, and Salman al-Farisi."
"485","[AI-translation] Asr. A man stood up to pray, so Umar saw him and said to him: ""Sit, for the People of the Book perished because there was no separation between their prayers."" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Ibn al-Khattab has done well."
"486","[AI-translation] Asr. A man stood up to pray, so Umar saw him and said to him: ""Sit, for the People of the Book perished because there was no separation between their prayers."" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Ibn al-Khattab has done well"
"487","[AI-translation] Asr. A man stood up to pray (after it), so Umar saw him, (and took hold of his cloak or his garment) and said to him: ""Sit, for the People of the Book perished because there was no separation between their prayers."" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Ibn al-Khattab has done well (and in a narration: has spoken the truth)."
"488","[AI-translation] From Samurah ibn Jundub that the Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Attend the dhikr and draw near to the Imam, for a man continues to move back until he is delayed in Paradise, even if he enters it."
"489","[AI-translation] From Hafsah who said: So we asked Umm Atiyyah: ""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him?"" She said: ""Yes, may my father be sacrificed for him - and whenever she narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, she would say: 'May my father be sacrificed for him' - I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Bring out the adolescent girls and the young women in seclusion, and let them witness the Eid and the supplication of the Muslims, and let the menstruating women keep away from the prayer place of the Muslims.'"
"490","Talq ibn Ali said: We went as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ, pledged allegiance to him, prayed with him, and informed him that we had a church in our land. We asked him for some of his leftover ablution water. He called for water, performed ablution, rinsed his mouth, then poured it into a water skin and commanded us, saying: ""Go forth, and when you reach your land, break down your church, sprinkle its place with this water, and make it a mosque."" They said: ""The land is far, the heat is severe, and the water will dry up?"" He said: ""Add water to it, for it will only increase it in goodness."" So we went until we arrived at our land, broke down our church, sprinkled its place, and made it a mosque. We called the adhan in it. He said: And the monk was a man from Tayy. When he heard the adhan, he said: ""A call of truth."" Then he faced a hill of our hills and we never saw him again."
"491","[AI-translation] From Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""When you come to the prayer, come to it with dignity and tranquility. Pray what you have caught, and make up what you have missed."
"492","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: ""If any one of you catches (the first) prostration of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, let him complete his prayer. And if he catches (the first) prostration of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, let him complete his prayer."
"493","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""If you catch a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises (and then it rises), then pray another one along with it."
"494","[AI-translation] From Abu Mahdhurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: ""When you give the Adhan for Maghrib, bring it down with the sun, bringing it down."
"495","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""When permission is sought from a man while he is praying, his permission is the tasbih. And when permission is sought from a woman while she is praying, her permission is the tasfiq."
"496","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik, reporting from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) who said: When the prayer is established and one of you is fasting, let him begin with the evening meal before the Maghrib prayer, and do not hasten away from your evening meal."
"497","[AI-translation] As who said: The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) enjoined upon me was: When you lead a people in prayer, make it light for them."
"498","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: When the reciter says Amin, say Amin, for the angels say Amin, and whoever's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven."
"499","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar, marfu'an (elevated to the Prophet): When the edge of the sun appears (in another wording: rises), delay the prayer until it is fully risen, and when the edge of the sun disappears, delay the prayer until it has set."
"500","[AI-translation] Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), who said: When one of you spits in the mosque, let him bury it, lest it strike the skin of a believer or his garment and harm him."
"501","[AI-translation] Narrated Busr bin Mihjan from his father Mihjan: He was sitting in an assembly with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) when the call for prayer was made. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) stood up and prayed, then returned, while Mihjan was still in his seat, having not prayed with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man?"" He said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but I had already prayed among my family."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""When you come, pray with the people, even if you have already prayed."
"502","[AI-translation] Narrated Kathir bin Qarwand who said: We asked Salim bin Abdullah about his father's prayer during travel. He reported from his father, Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When a matter presents itself to one of you which he fears missing, let him pray this prayer—meaning combining the two prayers."
"503","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When a Muslim goes out to the mosque, Allah records a good deed for him for every step he takes, and erases a bad deed from him by it, until he reaches his place of prayer."
"504","[AI-translation] Thaqafiyyah: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: When one of you goes out to the mosque, let her not approach perfume."
"505","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When a woman goes out to the mosque, let her wash from perfume as she would wash from janabah."
"506","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When the believers have been saved from the Fire and are secure, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of you will dispute with his companion regarding a right he has in this world more intensely than the believers will dispute with their Lord on behalf of their brothers who were admitted into the Fire.They will say: 'Our Lord, our brothers used to pray with us, fast with us, and perform Hajj with us (and fight alongside us), yet You admitted them into the Fire.'He will say: 'Go and bring out those whom you recognize among them.' So they will come to them and recognize them by their faces, for the Fire will not consume their faces. Some of them the Fire will have seized up to half their shins, and some up to their ankles. They will bring them out and say: 'Our Lord, we have brought out those You commanded us to.'Then He will say: 'Bring out those who had in their hearts the weight of a dinar of faith,' then 'those who had the weight of half a dinar,' until He says: 'Those who had the weight of an atom (dharr).'Abu Sa'id said: 'Whoever does not believe this, let him read this verse: ""Indeed, Allah does not wrong [even] an atom's weight; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward."" (An-Nisa: 40)Then they will say: 'Our Lord, we have brought out those You commanded us; no one with any good in him remains in the Fire.'Then Allah will say: 'The angels have interceded, the prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded, and there remains the Most Merciful of the merciful.'He will then take a handful from the Fire—or He said: two handfuls—of people who never did any good for Allah at all, who have been burnt until they became charcoal (humam). They will be brought to a water called the Water of Life, and it will be poured over them, and they will sprout as the seed sprouts in the silt left by a flood. They will emerge from their bodies like pearls, with seals on their necks [reading]: 'The Freed Ones of Allah.'It will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise. Whatever you wish for or see, it is yours, and with Me is even better than that.'They will say: 'Our Lord, what is better than that?'He will say: 'My Pleasure upon you, so I shall never be angry with you ever again.'"""
"507","[AI-translation] Zubayr on the minbar saying: When one of you enters the mosque and the people are in rukūʿ, let him bow when he enters, then let him shuffle forward bowing until he enters the row, for that is the Sunnah."
"508","[AI-translation] From Abū Hurayrah, that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was delivering the sermon on Friday when a man entered (and in a narration: ʿUthmān). ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Why do you hold back from the prayer?"" The man said: ""It is only that I heard the call and performed wuḍūʾ."" He said: ""Did you not hear the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: When one of you goes to Jumuʿah, let him perform ghusl?"
"509","[AI-translation] From Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, that a blind man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I hear the call, but perhaps I cannot find a guide?"" He said: ""When you hear the call, answer the caller of Allah, the Almighty and Majestic."
"510","[AI-translation] From Sahl ibn Muʿādh from his father from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, that he said: When you hear the caller making the call for the prayer, say as he says."
"511","[AI-translation] Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, saying: When one of you forgets in his prayer and does not know if he prayed one or two, let him build upon one. If he does not know if he prayed two or three, let him build upon two. And if he does not know if he prayed three or four, let him build upon three, and let him perform two prostrations before he gives the salām."
"512","[AI-translation] Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, saying: When one of you forgets in his prayer and does not know if he prayed one or two, let him build upon one. If he does not know if he prayed two or three, let him build upon two. And if he does not know if he prayed three or four, let him build upon three, and let him perform two prostrations before he gives the salām."
"513","[AI-translation] From Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When one of you prays towards a sutrah, let him draw near to it, so that Shayṭān does not pass between him and it."
"514","[AI-translation] Khaṭmī, marfūʿ: When one of you prays Jumuʿah, he should not pray anything after it until he speaks or leaves."
"515","[AI-translation] From Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When one of you prays, let him wear his two garments, for Allah is most deserving that one adorns oneself for Him."
"516","[AI-translation] From Muʿāwiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting."
"517","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Rabi' ibn Mu'awdh (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: When they pray over a funeral and speak well of him, the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: I have accepted their testimony regarding what they know, and I forgive him for what they do not know."
"518","On the authority of Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) and said: ""O Prophet of Allah! I ask you about something you know and I am ignorant of: Is there an hour of the night or day in which prayer is disliked?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you pray the dawn prayer (Fajr), then refrain from prayer until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. Then when it has risen, pray, for the prayer is witnessed and accepted until the sun is at its zenith like a spear. Then when it is at its zenith, that hour is when Hell is heated up and its gates are opened until it passes from your right eyebrow. Then when it has passed from your right eyebrow, pray, for the prayer is witnessed and accepted until you pray the afternoon prayer (Asr). Then leave prayer until the sun sets."""
"519","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Tariq ibn 'Abdullah from the Prophet (peace be upon him): When you pray, do not spit in front of you nor to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty, otherwise under your foot and rub it."
"520","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace be upon him): When one of you stands for prayer, he should not spit in front of him, for he is conversing with Allah as long as he is in his prayer, nor to his right, for there is an angel to his right, but he should spit to his left or under his foot and bury it."
"521","[AI-translation] Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: When one of you stands—or he said: when a man stands—in his prayer, Allah turns His face towards him, so let none of you spit towards his Qiblah, nor to his right, for the scribe of good deeds is on his right, but let him spit to his left."
"522","[AI-translation] Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When the imam stands up following the two rak'ahs, if he remembers before he stands fully upright, he should sit. But if he has already stood fully upright, he should not sit, and he should perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"523","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: When the companion of the Qur'an stands and recites it by night and day, he remembers it, but if he does not stand to recite it, he forgets it."
"524","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When the imam recites ""Not of those who have earned anger upon them, nor of those who are astray"" and the imam says Amin, then say Amin, for the angels say Amin upon his supplication, and whoever's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven."
"525","[AI-translation] Khudri from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: When one of you completes his prayer in his mosque, he should let his house have a share of his prayer, for Allah will place good in his house from his prayer."
"526","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Abdullah who said: We did not know what to say in every two rak'ahs except that we glorified, proclaimed the greatness, and praised our Lord. Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) taught us the openings of good and its conclusions. He said: When you sit in every two rak'ahs, say: All greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. Then let him choose from supplication what is most pleasing to him."
"527","[AI-translation] Ansari who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) and said: Advise me and be concise. He said: When you stand in your prayer, pray the prayer of one who is departing, do not speak any words you will have to apologize for tomorrow, and have complete despair of what is in the hands of people."
"528","[AI-translation] Samurah bin Jundub reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: When you stand for the prayer, do not precede your reciter in bowing and prostrating, but he should precede you."
"529","[AI-translation] A man from Juhainah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: When do I pray the last Isha? He said: When the night fills the belly of every valley, then pray the last Isha."
"530","[AI-translation] Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: If one of you dozes in the mosque on the day of Friday, let him move from that sitting place of his to another."
"531","[AI-translation] Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: When the call for prayer is made, the gates of heaven are opened and the supplication is answered."
"532","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Umar, elevated to the Prophet: If one of you passes wind while in his prayer, let him leave and perform ablution."
"533","[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Mughaffal reported that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: If you find the Imam prostrating, then prostrate; or bowing, then bow; or standing, then stand. And do not count the prostration if you do not catch the rak'ah."
"534","Qays ibn Talq narrated from his father Talq ibn Ali, who said: ""We went out as a delegation of six to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), five from Banu Hanifah and one man from Banu Dab'ah ibn Rabi'ah, until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). We pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him, and we informed him that we had a church in our land, and we asked him for some of his leftover ablution water. He called for water, performed ablution from it and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us into a water skin. Then he said: 'Go with this water, and when you arrive at your land, break down your church, sprinkle its place with this water, and make its place a mosque.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the land is far and the water will dry up.' He said: 'Add water to it, for it will only increase it in goodness.' So we went out and disputed over carrying the water skin — which of us would carry it? The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made it a rotation among us, for each man among us a day and a night. So we went out with it until we arrived at our land, and we did what he commanded us. The monk of that day was a man from Tayy. We called the adhan for prayer, and the monk said: 'A call of truth,' then he fled and we never saw him again."""
"535","[AI-translation] Uthman reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: What do you think if there was a river flowing in the courtyard of one of you, in which he bathes five times a day, would anything of his dirt remain? They said: Nothing. He said: Indeed, the prayers remove sins just as water removes dirt."
"536","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Salih, elevated and disconnected: Four rak'ahs before Dhuhr are equivalent to the pre-dawn prayer."
"537","[AI-translation] Jabir bin Abdullah reported: Sulayk Al-Ghatafani entered the mosque on the day of Friday while the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was addressing the people. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to him: Pray two rak'ahs, and do not ever return to something like this—meaning delaying in coming to the Friday prayer. He said: So he prayed them and then sat down."
"538","[AI-translation] Rabi' bin Sabrah bin Ma'bad, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Use a barrier in your prayer (and in a narration: Let one of you use a barrier in his prayer), even if it is with an arrow."
"539","[AI-translation] Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."
"540","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, saw a man praying while the muezzin was making the iqamah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Are there two prayers together?"
"541","[AI-translation] From Makhul, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, that he said: ""Seek the response of supplication at the meeting of the armies, the establishment of the prayer, and the falling of the rain."
"542","[AI-translation] Ibn Mas'ud reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: ""A servant among the servants of Allah was ordered to be struck in his grave with one hundred lashes. He did not cease asking and supplicating until it was reduced to a single lash. He was struck a single lash, and his grave was filled with fire. When it was lifted from him and he regained consciousness, he said: 'Why did you beat me?' They said: 'You performed a prayer without purification, and you passed by an oppressed person and did not help him.'"
"543","[AI-translation] Yamani said: I said to Ibn Abbas, ""They claim that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: 'Perform the ritual bath on Friday, and wash your heads even if you are not in a state of major ritual impurity, and apply some perfume.'"" Ibn Abbas said: ""As for the perfume, I do not know, but as for the ritual bath, yes."
"544","[AI-translation] Anas said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, ""O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah, Mighty and Majestic, obligated upon His servants?"" He said: ""Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, is there anything before them or after them?"" He said: ""Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers"" (he said this three times). The man swore by Allah that he would neither add anything to it nor subtract anything from it. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""If he is truthful, he will surely enter Paradise."
"545","[AI-translation] Ibn Umar said to Humran ibn Aban: ""What prevents you from praying in congregation?"" He said: ""I have already prayed the Fajr prayer in congregation on Friday."" He said: ""Has it not reached you that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: 'The most virtuous prayers in the sight of Allah is the Fajr prayer on Friday in congregation.'"
"546","[AI-translation] Uqbah ibn Amir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to me: ""Recite the Mu'awwidhat at the end of every prayer."
"547","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Straighten the rows in the prayer, for straightening the rows is part of the perfection of the prayer."
"548","[AI-translation] From Abu Shajarah, traced back to the Prophet: ""Straighten the rows, for you align yourselves like the rows of the angels. Align between the shoulders, fill the gaps, and do not leave openings for Satan. And whoever connects a row, Allah will connect him."
"549","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, sent an expedition, and they acquired abundant spoils and made a swift return. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen an expedition of any people with a swifter return or greater spoils than this expedition. He said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Shall I not inform you of a swifter return and greater spoils than this expedition? A man performs ablution in his house and perfects his ablution, then sets out for the mosque, prays the morning prayer in it, and follows it with the Duha prayer. He has indeed made a swift return and acquired great spoils."
"550","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr who said: It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family—and perhaps Sufyan said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! The people of wealth and riches have taken the reward; they say as we say, and they spend while we do not spend. He said to me: Shall I not inform you of a matter which, if you do it, you will catch up with those who preceded you and surpass those who come after you? You praise Allah, glorify Him, and magnify Him thirty-three, thirty-three, and thirty-four times at the end of every prayer."
"551","[AI-translation] From Rafi' bin Khadij who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He delays the Asr prayer until, when the sun is like the thigh of a cow, he prays it."
"552","Auf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), nine or eight or seven in number, when he said: ""Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah?"" We had recently pledged allegiance, so we said: ""We have already pledged allegiance to you, O Messenger of Allah."" Then he said again: ""Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah?"" We said: ""We have already pledged allegiance to you, O Messenger of Allah."" Then he said a third time: ""Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah?"" So we stretched out our hands and said: ""We have pledged allegiance to you, O Messenger of Allah, but on what basis shall we pledge allegiance to you?"" He said: ""On the basis that you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, perform the five prayers, obey"" — and he whispered a subtle word — ""and do not ask people for anything."" I saw some of those men drop their whips, yet none of them would ask anyone to hand it back to him."
"553","[AI-translation] From Talhah bin Ubaydullah, may Allah be pleased with him: Two men from Bali, a tribe from Quda'ah, were such that one was killed in the cause of Allah, and the other died a year later. Talhah said: I saw in a dream that Paradise was opened, and I saw the latter of the two men enter Paradise before the first. I was amazed, so when I woke up I mentioned it, and it reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Did he not fast Ramadan after him? And pray six rak'ahs after him, and such and such rak'ahs for the prayer of the end of the year?"
"554","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, that he said: A servant from among the servants of Allah was ordered to be struck a hundred lashes in his grave. He continued to ask and supplicate until it became a single lash. He was struck a single lash, and his grave was filled with fire. When it was lifted from him and he came to, he said: ""Why did you strike me?"" They said: ""You prayed a single prayer without purification, and you passed by a wronged person and did not help him."
"555","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abu Bakr: ""At what time do you pray Witr?"" He said: ""At the beginning of the night after Isha."" He said: ""And you, O Umar?"" He said: ""At the end of the night."" The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""As for you, O Abu Bakr, you have taken the firmer hold, and as for you, O Umar, you have taken with strength."
"556","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: Banu Salamah were in the outskirts of Madinah, and they wanted to move closer to the mosque. Then this verse was revealed: ""Indeed, it is We who bring the dead to life, and record what they have put forth and their traces."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Your traces are recorded."" He said: So they did not move."
"557","[AI-translation] From a man from Banu Bayadah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, observed I'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan, and said: ""When one of you is in prayer, he is only whispering to his Lord, so do not raise your voices with the Quran lest you harm the believers."
"558","[AI-translation] Jayshani: Amr bin al-As addressed the people on Friday and said: Abu Basrah told me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: ""Allah has added a prayer for you, and it is Witr. Pray it between the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer."" Abu Tamim said: Abu Dharr took me by the hand and walked with me to the mosque to Abu Basrah and said to him: ""Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say what Amr said?"" Abu Basrah said: ""I heard it from the Messenger of Allah."
"559","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has added a prayer to your prayers which is better for you than red camels. Verily, it is the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer."
"560","[AI-translation] Khattab, marfu'an: Verily, Allah is amazed at the prayer in congregation."
"561","[AI-translation] From Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Allah will call out on the Day of Resurrection: 'Where are My neighbors? Where are My neighbors?' He said: So the angels will say: 'Our Lord, and who is worthy of being Your neighbor?' He will say: 'Where are the maintainers of the mosques?'"
"562","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), he said: ""Verily, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who connect the rows."
"563","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who connect the rows, and whoever fills a gap, Allah raises him by it a degree."
"564","[AI-translation] Bara', he said: We were sitting, waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) (in the Musalla) on the Day of Al-Adha. He came and greeted the people with salam, and said: ""The first mansak (and in a narration: nusuk) of this day of yours is the prayer."" He stepped forward and led the people in two rak'ahs, then said the salam and faced the people. Then he was given a bow, or a stick, and he leaned on it. He praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, extolled Him, commanded them, and forbade them."
"565","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Allah will resurrect the days on the Day of Resurrection in their forms, and He will resurrect Friday radiant and luminous. Its people will surround it like a bride being led to her noble husband; it will shine for them, and they will walk in its light. Their colors will be white like snow, and their fragrance will spread like musk. They will wade through the mountains of camphor. The two weighty ones will look at them in amazement, not blinking, until they enter Paradise. No one will mix with them except the mu'adhdhins who seek reward."
"566","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), that he said: ""Verily, the best of what mounts are ridden to is this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."
"567","[AI-translation] From Hudhaifah, that he saw Shabath bin Rab'iyy spitting in front of him, so he said: ""O Shabath! Do not spit in front of you, for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to forbid that, and he said: 'Verily, when a man stands to pray, Allah turns His face towards him until he turns away or an evil occurrence takes place.'"
"568","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: ""Verily, a man may pray for sixty years and not a single prayer of his is accepted; perhaps he perfects the bowing and does not perfect the prostration, and perfects the prostration and does not perfect the bowing."
"569","[AI-translation] Laithi, the Companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), during the illness in which he died. He said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer upon the people, and the most constant in it for himself. And in a narration: and the longest of people in prayer for himself."
"570","[AI-translation] Zuhri (mursalan) that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to go out on the day of Fitr, pronouncing takbir until he reached the prayer place and until he concluded the prayer. When he concluded the prayer, he would stop the takbir."
"571","[AI-translation] From Hilal bin Yasaf who said: I arrived in al-Raqqa and one of my companions said to me, ""Would you like [to see] a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him?"" He said: I said, ""A windfall."" So we went to Wabisa. I said to my companion, ""Let us begin by looking at his appearance."" He had on a close-fitting cap with two earflaps, and a dusty-brown silken hooded cloak, and he was leaning on a staff in his prayer. We said to him after we had greeted him with salam, and he said: ""Umm Qays bint Mihsan narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, when he grew old and gained flesh, set up a pillar in his prayer place to lean upon."
"572","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""When the devil hears the call to prayer, he goes until he reaches al-Rawha."
"573","ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated from his father, from his grandfather Qatādah ibn al-Nuʿmān, who said: ""It was a night of intense darkness and rain. I said to myself: 'Would that I took advantage of this night to attend the ʿIshāʾ prayer with the Prophet ﷺ!' So I did. When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer and turned to leave, he noticed me while he was walking with a dried palm-stalk (ʿurjūn) in his hand. He said: 'What brings you here at this hour, O Qatādah?' I replied: 'I took advantage of attending the prayer with you, O Messenger of Allah.' He gave me the palm-stalk and said: 'Indeed, Satan has stayed behind in your home. Go with this palm-stalk, hold onto it until you reach your house, then take it from behind the house and strike with it.' I left the mosque, and the palm-stalk lit up like a candle, giving light by which I walked. I came to my family and found them asleep. I looked into the corner and found a hedgehog there. I kept striking it with the palm-stalk until it went out."""
"574","On the authority of Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: I was a young, unmarried man during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so I used to sleep in the mosque. Whoever among us saw a dream would relate it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So I said: ""O Allah, if there is any good for me with You, then show me a dream that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will interpret for me."" I fell asleep and saw two angels come to me; they took me along. Another angel met them and said: ""Do not be afraid."" Then they took me to the Fire, and behold, it was folded up like the folding of a well, and there were people in it whom I recognized some of them. Then they took me to the right side. When morning came, I mentioned that to Ḥafṣa. Ḥafṣa claimed that she related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: ""ʿAbdullāh is a righteous man; if only he would pray more at night."" He said: So ʿAbdullāh used to pray more at night."
"575","On the authority of Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was a young, unmarried man during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so I would stay overnight in the mosque. Whoever among us saw a dream would narrate it to the Prophet (peace be upon him). I said: ""O Allah, if there is any good for me with You, then show me a dream that the Prophet (peace be upon him) may interpret for me."" So I slept and saw two angels coming to me; they took me away. Another angel met them and said: ""Have no fear."" Then they took me to the Fire. Behold, it was folded up like the folding of a well, and therein were people whom I recognized some of. Then they took me to the right side. When morning came, I mentioned that to Hafsa. Hafsa reported that she had narrated it to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he said: ""Abdullah is a righteous man, would that he prayed more at night."" He (the narrator) said: So Abdullah used to pray more at night."
"576","[AI-translation] From Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: He, peace be upon him and his family, commanded us to use the siwak and said: ""When the servant stands to pray, the angel comes and stands behind him, listening to the Quran and drawing near. He continues to listen and draw near until he places his mouth upon his mouth. Thus, he does not recite a verse except that it is inside the angel."
"577","Abu Hurairah reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Prayer has a beginning and an end. The beginning of the time for the Zuhr prayer is when the sun passes its zenith, and its end is when the time for the Asr prayer enters. The beginning of the time for the Asr prayer is when its time enters, and its end is when the sun turns yellow. The beginning of the time for the Maghrib prayer is when the sun sets, and its end is when the twilight disappears. The beginning of the time for the Isha prayer is when the twilight disappears, and its end is when half the night has passed. The beginning of the time for the Fajr prayer is when dawn breaks, and its end is when the sun rises."""
"578","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""The mosques have pegs; the angels are their sitters. If they are absent, the angels miss them; if they are sick, the angels visit them; and if they are in need, the angels help them."" And he, peace be upon him, said: ""The sitter in the mosque is upon three traits: a newly acquired brother, a firm word, or an awaited mercy."
"579","[AI-translation] Farsi who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""When the Muslim prays, his sins are suspended above his head. Every time he prostrates, they fall away from him. Thus, he finishes his prayer, and his sins have fallen away."
"580","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah and Aishah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, that he peered out from his room while the people were praying, raising their voices in recitation, and he said to them: ""The one praying is whispering to his Lord, so let him consider what he whispers to Him, and do not raise your voices over one another in the Quran."
"581","[AI-translation] From Thawban who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, on a journey, and he said: ""This journey is a strain and a burden. When one of you prays Witr, let him pray two rak'ahs. If he wakes up, well and good; but if not, they are counted for him."
"582","[AI-translation] Ghifari who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, led us in the Asr prayer at al-Mukhammas, and said: ""This prayer was presented to those before you, but they wasted it. Whoever observes it will have its reward twice. And there is no prayer after it until the witness rises."" The witness is the star."
"583","[AI-translation] From Anas that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The Jews envy you for the salam and the amin."
"584","[AI-translation] Khudri, that a man greeted the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, while he was in prayer, so the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, responded with a gesture. When he pronounced the salam, the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to him: ""We used to return the greeting in our prayer, but we were forbidden from doing so."
"585","[AI-translation] From Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, stood up in the night, and a woman was praying following his prayer. When he sensed her, he turned to her and said to her: ""Lie down if you wish."" She said: ""I feel energetic."" He said: ""You are not like me, for the coolness of my eyes has been placed in prayer."
"586","[AI-translation] Maqburi, that Abu Basra Jamil bin Basra met Abu Hurayrah while he was coming from al-Tur, so he said: ""Had I met you before you went to it, you would not have gone to it. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: 'The mounts are only driven to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque.'"
"587","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""The likeness of the one who sets out early for the prayer is like the one who offers a she-camel, then the one who follows him is like the one who offers a cow, then the one who follows him is like the one who offers a ram, then the one who follows him is like the one who offers a chicken, then the one who follows him is like the one who offers an egg."
"588","[AI-translation] Agharr al-Muzani, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: ""O Prophet of Allah, I have entered the morning and did not pray Witr."" He said: ""Witr is only at night."" He said: ""O Prophet of Allah, I have entered the morning and did not pray Witr."" He said: ""Then pray Witr."
"589","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""So-and-so prays at night, but when morning comes he steals."" He said: ""What he says will soon prevent him."
"590","[AI-translation] From 'Ata bin Yasar, from a man of the Ansar from the tribe of Bani Bayada, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, while he was observing i'tikaf in the mosque one day, admonishing the people, warning them, and encouraging them. Then he said: ""There is no one who prays except that he is whispering to his Lord, so let not some of you raise your voices over others in recitation."
"591","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, had a khamisa, which he gave to Abu Juhm. It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! This khamisa is better than the anbijaniyya!"" He said: ""It distracts me from my prayer,"" or he said, ""It preoccupies me."
"592","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh bin Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, prayed one day a prayer and made it long. When he finished, we said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you made the prayer long today?"" He said: ""I prayed a prayer of hope and fear. I asked Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, for three things for my Ummah, and He gave me two and returned one to me. I asked Him not to let an enemy from outside of them overpower them, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to destroy them by drowning, and He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to make their fighting among themselves, but He returned it to me."
"593","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""I have grown bulky, so when I bow, bow, and when I rise, rise, and when I prostrate, prostrate. And let me not find a man preceding me to bowing or to prostration."
"594","[AI-translation] From Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, prayed Witr with five, and prayed Witr with seven."
"595","[AI-translation] From Anas, elevated to the Prophet: The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last of it is the prayer."
"596","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: The prayer was first prescribed as two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. So when he, peace be upon him and his family, arrived in Madinah, he added to every prayer the like of it, except Maghrib, for it is the Witr of the day, and the Fajr prayer because of the length of its recitation. And when he traveled, he returned to his original prayer."
"597","[AI-translation] From Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The first thing a servant will be held accountable for is the prayer, and the first thing judged between the people will be regarding bloodshed."
"598","[AI-translation] From Anas, elevated to the Prophet: The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. If it is sound, the rest of his deeds will be sound for him, and if it is corrupted, the rest of his deeds will be corrupted."
"599","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Beware of the gaps, meaning in the prayer."
"600","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Any woman who has applied incense, let her not attend the Isha prayer with us."
"601","[AI-translation] From Hazim who said: Sahl bin Sa'd al-Sa'idi used to put forward the young men of his people to lead them in prayer. It was said to him: You do this, while you have the precedence you have? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: The imam is responsible. If he does well, then it is for him and for them, and if he does poorly, meaning, then it is against him and against them."
"602","[AI-translation] Farisi, elevated to the Prophet: Blessing is in three: in the congregation, in Tharid, and in the pre-dawn meal."
"603","[AI-translation] From a man among the Companions of Muhammad, peace be upon him and his family, who said: A man's voluntary prayer in his house increases over his voluntary prayer among the people, like the superiority of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone."
"604","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Dharr from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""The prayer is repeated due to the passing of a donkey, a woman, and a black dog."" I (Abdullah ibn Samit) asked: ""What is the case of the black dog from the yellow dog from the red dog?"" He said: ""I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) as you asked me, and he said: 'The black dog is a devil.'"
"605","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah from the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""The congregational prayer surpasses the prayer of one of you alone by twenty-five parts, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day meet together in the Fajr prayer."
"606","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: That is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace be upon him), meaning the completion of the prayer by the traveler when he prays behind a resident, otherwise it is shortened."
"607","[AI-translation] Narrated from a man of the Ansar among the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him), elevating it to the Prophet: ""Three are a duty upon every Muslim: performing Ghusl on Friday, using the Siwak, and applying some perfume if one finds it."
"608","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: ""Three things, all of which are a duty upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending the funeral, and responding to the sneezer when he praises Allah—Mighty and Majestic."
"609","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Three are under the guarantee of Allah—Mighty and Majestic: a man who goes out to a mosque from the mosques of Allah—Mighty and Majestic, a man who goes out as a warrior in the path of Allah, and a man who goes out as a pilgrim."
"610","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas ibn Malik, elevating it to the Prophet: ""Three from whom no prayer is accepted, nor does it ascend to the heaven, nor does it pass beyond their heads: a man who leads a people who dislike him, a man who prays over a funeral without being ordered, and a woman whose husband calls her at night but she refuses him."
"611","[AI-translation] Muhammad ibn Ismail said: It was said to Abdullah ibn Abi Habibah: ""Did you reach the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" He said: ""The Messenger of Allah came to our mosque in Quba. I came as a young boy (prepubescent) and sat on his right (and Abu Bakr sat on his left). Then he called for a drink, drank from it, and then gave it to me while I was on his right, so I drank from it. Then he stood to pray, and I saw him praying in his sandals."
"612","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas ibn Malik, elevating it to the Prophet: ""My comfort of the eyes has been placed in the prayer."
"613","[AI-translation] Mughirah ibn Shubah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""My comfort of the eyes has been placed in the prayer."
"614","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: Friday to Friday is an expiation for whatever is between them, as long as the major sins are not committed."
"615","[AI-translation] Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me, and among what he taught me, he said to me: ""Guard the five prayers."" I said: ""These are times in which I have preoccupations, so command me with a comprehensive act which, if I do it, will suffice me."" He said: ""Guard the two 'Asrs: a prayer before the rising of the sun, and a prayer before its setting."
"616","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Umamah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) returned from Khaybar accompanied by two slave boys. 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Messenger of Allah, give us one to serve us."" He said: ""Take whichever of them you wish."" He said: ""Choose for me."" He said: ""Take this one and do not beat him, for I saw him praying as we were coming from Khaybar, and I have been forbidden from striking those who pray."" And he gave the other slave boy to Abu Dharr and said: ""Treat him well."" Then he said: ""O Abu Dharr! What did the slave boy whom I gave you do?"" He said: ""You commanded me to treat him well, so I freed him."
"617","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn 'Umar, elevated to the Prophet: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) went out to Quba to pray there. The Ansar came and greeted him with salam while he was praying. He [Ibn 'Umar] said: I said to Bilal: ""How did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) reply to them when they greeted him with salam while he was praying?"" He said: ""He did like this,"" and he spread his palm. Ja'far ibn 'Awn spread his palm, making its underside face downward and its back face upward."
"618","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, marfūʿan: ""Six characteristics: no Muslim dies while engaged in one of them except that it is guaranteed upon Allah to admit him into Paradise: a man who goes out fighting in Allah's cause—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who follows a funeral procession—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who visits a sick person—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who performs ablution and perfects it, then goes out to the mosque for his prayer—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; a man who comes to an imām, not coming to him except to excuse him and honor him—if he dies in that state, it is guaranteed upon Allah; and a man in his house who does not backbite a Muslim, nor bring upon them wrath or punishment—if he dies, it is guaranteed upon Allah."""
"619","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) passed by a grave of someone recently buried and said: ""Two light rak'ahs from what you take lightly and perform as supererogatory, which this one adds to his deeds, are more beloved to him than the remainder of your world."
"620","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Bakrah: He came while the Messenger of Allah was in ruku', so he performed ruku' short of the row, then walked to the row. When the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) concluded his prayer, he said: ""Which of you is the one who performed ruku' short of the row and then walked to the row?"" Abu Bakrah said: ""I."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""May Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat it."
"621","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice in the prayer for every addition and omission."
"622","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah, elevated to the Prophet: The honor of the believer is his prayer at night, and his pride is his independence from what is in the hands of people."
"623","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn 'Abbas, who said: He led us in prayer in Madinah eight and seven: Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha'."
"624","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah ibn Buhaynah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) led us in one of the prayers (in a narration: the Zuhr prayer), and he stood up after two [rak'ahs] (and did not sit). So he was prompted with tasbih (when he straightened up, he proceeded and did not go back). (The people stood up with him). He continued until (when) he finished his prayer, and nothing remained but the salam (and the people waited for his salam), he performed two prostrations (saying takbir in each prostration, while sitting) before he gave salam (then he gave salam). (And the people prostrated with him, in place of the sitting he had forgotten)."
"625","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, he says: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Narrate a hadith to me and make it concise."" The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to him: ""Pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, as if you see Him; for if you do not see Him, He sees you. Despair of what is in people's hands, you will live rich, and beware of that which requires an excuse."
"626","[AI-translation] Qasim al-Shaybani that Zayd ibn Arqam saw a group of people praying during the forenoon, so he said: ""Have they not known that prayer in other than this hour is better? The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: The prayer of the oft-repentant is when the young camels' hooves feel the heat of the sun."
"627","[AI-translation] From Amr ibn Abasah, raised to the Prophet: The night prayer is two by two, and the latter part of the night is more responsive to supplication. He said: I said: ""More responsive?"" He said: ""No, rather most responsive,"" meaning by that the answering."
"628","[AI-translation] Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees. If he prays it in a barren land and perfects its ablution, bowing, and prostration, his prayer reaches fifty degrees."
"629","[AI-translation] Laythi, raised to the Prophet: The prayer of two men, one of whom leads his companion, is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of eight praying individually, and the prayer of four, one of whom leads them, is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of a hundred praying individually."
"630","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet: The prayer of the one sitting is half of the prayer of the one standing."
"631","[AI-translation] Arqam (from his grandfather al-Arqam) who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he said to me: ""Where are you heading?"" I said: ""To Bayt al-Maqdis."" He said: ""For trade?"" I said: ""No, but I intended to pray in it."" He said: ""A prayer here""—meaning al-Madinah—""is better than a thousand prayers here""—meaning Ilya."
"632","[AI-translation] From Abu Ayyub from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, raised to him: Pray the Maghrib prayer with the setting of the sun, racing against the appearance of the star."
"633","[AI-translation] From Anas and Jabir who both said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Pray in your houses, and do not abandon the voluntary prayers in them."
"634","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, raised to the Prophet: Pray in the sheepfolds and wipe away their dust, for they are from the beasts of Paradise."
"635","[AI-translation] Muzani that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, prayed two rak'ahs before Maghrib, then said: ""Pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib."" Then he said a third time: ""For whoever wishes,"" fearing that the people would reckon it a Sunnah."
"636","[AI-translation] 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, combined [prayers] between the first [Dhuhr] and 'Asr, and between Maghrib and 'Isha. It was said to him, and he said: ""I did this so that my Ummah would not face hardship."
"637","[AI-translation] Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I saw 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ""kneading"" in the prayer, leaning on his hands when he stood up. I said: ""What is this, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?"" He said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, 'kneading' in the prayer."
"638","[AI-translation] 'As who said: The last words the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, spoke to me when he appointed me over Ta'if were: ""Lighten the prayer for the people, to the point of 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' (al-A'la), 'Read in the name of your Lord who created' (al-'Alaq), and their like from the Qur'an."
"639","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, visited a sick man among his companions, and I was with him. He entered upon him while he was praying on a staff, placing his forehead on the staff. He gestured to him, so he discarded the staff and took a cushion. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Put it away from you. If you are able to prostrate on the earth, do so; otherwise, gesture, and make your prostration lower than your bowing."
"640","[AI-translation] No, but shake hands,"" meaning: he does not bow to his friend... nor kiss him when he meets him. From Anas ibn Malik who said: A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, when one of us meets his friend, does he bow to him?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""No."" He said: ""Does he embrace him and kiss him?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Does he shake his hand?"" He said: ""Yes, if he wishes."" This is the context of Ahmad, and likewise al-Tirmidhi, but he does not have [the words] ""if he wishes."
"641","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer, and no step has a greater reward than a step a man takes toward a gap in the row and fills it."
"642","[AI-translation] From Umm Salama, raised to the Prophet: ""The best mosques for women are their houses."
"643","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The prayer is three thirds: purification is a third, bowing is a third, and prostration is a third. So whoever fulfills it with its right, it is accepted from him, and the rest of his deeds are accepted from him. And whoever has his prayer rejected, the rest of his deeds are rejected upon him."
"644","[AI-translation] From a man among the companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was asked: ""Which deed is most virtuous?"" He said: ""Prayer at its appointed time, dutifulness to parents, and Jihad."
"645","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The five prayers are expiations for what is between them, provided major sins are avoided, and Friday to Friday, plus three days."
"646","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to say: The five prayers, and Friday to Friday, and Ramadan to Ramadan, are expiations for what is between them, if the major sins are avoided."
"647","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace be upon him) came upon a man prostrating on his face without placing his nose. He said: ""Place your nose, it should prostrate with you."
"648","On the authority of Abu Musa, who said: ""I and my companions who had arrived with me on the ship were staying at Baqi' Buthan, while the Prophet ﷺ was in Medina. A group from among them would take turns waiting for the Prophet ﷺ at the time of the Isha prayer every night. It so happened that my companions and I coincided with the Prophet ﷺ, but he had some occupation regarding some of his affairs, so he delayed the prayer until the middle of the night. Then the Prophet ﷺ came out and led them in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he said to those present: 'Take it easy! Rejoice, for it is from Allah's favor upon you that no one among the people is praying at this hour except you,' or he said: 'No one has prayed this prayer except you.' He (the narrator) said: 'He does not know which of the two statements he said.' Abu Musa said: 'So we returned rejoicing at what we had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'His saying: (Ibharra) means: it became the middle. And the 'Buhra' of everything is its middle. It was said: (Ibhar al-layl) is when its stars appear and it becomes illuminated; the first (meaning) is more common."""
"649","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, that the Prophet said: In every two rak'ahs there is a tashahhud and salutation upon the Messengers, and upon those who followed them among the righteous servants of Allah."
"650","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The dawn is two dawns: a dawn in which food is forbidden and prayer is permitted, and a dawn in which prayer is forbidden and food is permitted."
"651","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The dawn is two dawns: a dawn called the tail of the wolf, which is the false one, it extends lengthwise and does not extend widthwise; and the latter dawn extends widthwise and does not extend lengthwise."
"652","[AI-translation] From Abu Qatadah bin Ribi'i, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I have enjoined upon your nation five prayers, and I have made a covenant with Myself that whoever maintains them at their appointed times, I will admit him to Paradise, but whoever does not maintain them, there is no covenant for him with Me."
"653","[AI-translation] Khudri, who said: It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the flank of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) while he was prostrating."
"654","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), when he intended to prostrate, would say the takbeer, then prostrate; and when he rose from the sitting position, he would say the takbeer, then rise."
"655","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik: When he (peace be upon him and his family) began the prayer, he would say: ""Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, and blessed is Your Name, and exalted is Your Majesty, and there is no deity other than You."
"656","[AI-translation] Ashja'i, from his father (Tariq bin Ashyam), who said: When a man accepted Islam, the first thing he would teach us was the prayer, or he said: he taught him the prayer."
"657","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), whenever he was pleased with a man, would command him to pray."
"658","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) finished the morning prayer, he would say: ""Did any of you see a dream tonight?"" and he would say: ""There remains no prophecy after me except the good dream."
"659","[AI-translation] Zubayr: The Prophet (peace be upon him), when he sat in the second or the fourth, would place his hands on his knees, then point with his finger."
"660","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), whenever he raised his head from bowing in the morning prayer in the last rak'ah, would perform the Qunut."
"661","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), when he bowed, if water were poured on his back it would settle."
"662","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: She said: When he uttered the salam, he would not sit except for the amount of time it takes to say: ""O Allah, You are Peace, and from You comes Peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honour."
"663","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Rafi': The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), whenever he heard the Mu'adhdhin, would say what he said, until he reached ""Come to prayer, come to success,"" whereupon he would say: ""There is no power and no strength except with Allah."
"664","On the authority of ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, who said: We asked ʿAlī about the voluntary prayers of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) during the day. He said: ""You cannot bear it."" We said: ""Inform us of it, that we may take from it what we can bear."" He said: ""When he prayed Fajr, he would wait until the sun was from here"" — meaning from the direction of the east — ""the measure of it from the ʿAṣr prayer from here"" — meaning from the direction of the west — ""then he would stand and pray two rakʿahs. Then he would wait until the sun was from here"" — meaning from the direction of the east — ""the measure of it from the Ẓuhr prayer from here"" — meaning from the direction of the west — ""then he would stand and pray four, and four before Ẓuhr when the sun passed its zenith, and two rakʿahs after it, and four before ʿAṣr, separating between every two rakʿahs with the taslīm upon the angels brought near, the prophets, and those who followed them from the Muslims, (he would make the taslīm at the end of it)."""
"665","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Samurah: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), whenever he prayed the Fajr, would sit cross-legged in his place until the sun rose."
"666","On the authority of Suhayb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to whisper when he prayed. He said: ""Did you notice that? I remembered a prophet from among the prophets who was given soldiers from his people. He said: 'Who will match these, or who will fight these?' Or words to that effect. Then Allah revealed to him: 'Choose for your people one of three: that I empower an enemy over them, or hunger, or death.' So he consulted his people concerning that. They said: 'We entrust that to you; you are the Prophet of Allah.' So he stood and prayed—and when they were stricken with fear, they would resort to prayer. He said: 'O Lord, as for hunger or the enemy, then no; but death.' So death was empowered over them for three days, and seventy thousand of them died. The whispering you see me utter is: 'O Allah, by You I fight, and by You I assault, and there is no power and no strength except by You.'"""
"667","[AI-translation] Narrated Alqamah bin Wa'il, from his father: That the Prophet (peace be upon him), when he stood in prayer, would grasp his left with his right."
"668","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah reported: When the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) stood up at night to offer Tahajjud, he would pray two light Rak'ahs."
"669","[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Mas'ud reported: The Prophet (peace be upon him), when he was bowing or prostrating, would say: ""Glory be to You and praise be to You, I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You."
"670","[AI-translation] Hunai reported: I asked Anas bin Malik about shortening the prayer - and I used to go out to Kufa and pray two Rak'ahs until I returned - so Anas said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) traveled a distance of three miles or three Farsakh (Shu'bah doubted), he would shorten the prayer. In another narration: (he prayed two Rak'ahs)."
"671","On the authority of Suhayb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to whisper something during prayer that I could not understand, and he would not inform us of it. He said: ""Did you notice me?"" We said: ""Yes."" He said: ""I recalled a prophet from among the prophets who was given soldiers from his people (and in another narration: he was amazed by his nation), so he said: 'Who will match these?' or 'Who will stand up to these?' or other words to that effect (and in the other narration: 'Who will stand up to these?' without doubt). It was revealed to him: 'Choose for your people one of three: either we empower an enemy from other than them over them, or hunger, or death.' He consulted his people concerning that. They said: 'You are the Prophet of Allah, so all of that is up to you; choose for us.' He stood for prayer, and when they were panic-stricken they would resort to prayer. He prayed as Allah willed. Then he said: 'O my Lord! As for an enemy from other than them, then no; or hunger, then no; but death.' So death was empowered over them, and seventy thousand of them died in a single day. The whispering you see me utter is: 'O Allah, by You I maneuver, by You I advance, and by You...' [the text ends abruptly]."""
"672","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah reported: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) finished reciting Umm al-Qur'an, he would raise his voice and say ""Ameen""."
"673","[AI-translation] Aishah reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) would pass by the cooking pot, take the meat on the bone, eat from it, and then pray without performing ablution and without touching water. (In another narration: he did not perform ablution nor rinse his mouth)."
"674","[AI-translation] Mu'adh bin Jabal reported: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) during the expedition of Tabuk, if he departed before the sun declined, would delay Dhuhr until he combined it with Asr, and would pray them both together. And if he departed after the sun had declined, he would hasten Asr to Dhuhr and pray Dhuhr and Asr together, then he would travel. And if he departed before Maghrib, he would delay Maghrib until he prayed it with Isha. And if he departed after Maghrib, he would hasten Isha and pray it with Maghrib."
"675","[AI-translation] Awn bin Abi Juhaifah reported from his father: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was on a journey in which they slept until the sun rose, so he said: ""You were dead, and Allah returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps through a prayer, let him pray it when he wakes up, and whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it."
"676","[AI-translation] Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Mu'adhdhin would give the Adhan for the Maghrib prayer during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), and the core of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) would rush to the pillars to pray the two Rak'ahs before Maghrib until the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came out while they were praying. (A stranger would come and think that the prayer had already been prayed due to the large number of those praying them), (and there was a short interval between the Adhan and the Iqamah)."
"677","[AI-translation] Abdullah reported: Your Prophet, when he was bowing or prostrating, would say: ""Glory be to You and praise be to You, I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You."
"678","[AI-translation] Muntashir reported from his father that he used to pray two Rak'ahs after Asr. He was asked about it, so he said: ""If I were to pray them only because I saw Masruq praying them, that would be reliable enough, but I asked Aishah and she said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) did not abandon the two Rak'ahs before Fajr and the two Rak'ahs after Asr.'"
"679","[AI-translation] From Aishah: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used not to pray in our blankets."
"680","[AI-translation] From Anas: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used not to perform Qunut except when he supplicated for a people or supplicated against a people."
"681","[AI-translation] Zubayr, from whoever narrated to him among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), who said: He used to command us to establish mosques in our houses, and to maintain their structure, and to purify them."
"682","[AI-translation] From Abu Said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to combine the two prayers during travel."
"683","[AI-translation] Ashari: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to love for the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be near him so they could memorize from him."
"684","[AI-translation] From Imran bin Husayn he said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to narrate to us for most of the night about the Children of Israel, and he would not stand except for the length of a prayer."
"685","[AI-translation] Nadr: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to go out after the call to prayer to the mosque, and if he saw the people of the mosque were few, he would sit until he saw a group among them, then he would pray. And when he went out and saw a group, he would establish the prayer."
"686","[AI-translation] Khudri: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to go out on the day of Al-Adha and the day of Al-Fitr, and would begin with the prayer. When he had prayed his prayer and given salam, he would stand (standing) (on his feet) and turn toward the people (with his face) while they were sitting in their prayer place. If he had a need regarding an expedition, he would mention it to the people, or if he had a need other than that, he would command them concerning it. And he used to say, ""Give charity, give charity, give charity."" And the majority of those who gave charity were the women, then he would depart."
"687","[AI-translation] Zubayr, from his father: That the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to deliver the khutbah leaning on a staff in his hand."
"688","[AI-translation] Bara bin Azib: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to prostrate on the two fleshy parts of his palms."
"689","[AI-translation] From Anas: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to utter one taslim."
"690","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abza that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to point with his index finger in the prayer."
"691","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha who said: He (peace be upon him) used to pray in Makkah two rak'ahs - meaning: the obligatory prayers. When he arrived in Madinah, and the prayer was prescribed upon him as four and three, he prayed [them] and left the two rak'ahs he used to pray in Makkah as completion for the traveler."
"692","[AI-translation] Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) was praying with them one day, and a woman passed by al-Batha'. He gestured to her to step back, so she returned until he finished praying, then she passed by."
"693","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) was praying near the Maqam, and Abu Jahl ibn Hisham passed by him and said: ""O Muhammad! Did I not forbid you from this?!"" and he threatened him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) spoke harshly to him and rebuked him. He said: ""O Muhammad! With what do you threaten me?! By Allah, I have the most numerous retinue in this valley."" So Allah revealed: ""Let him call his retinue, We will call the Zabaniyah"" (Al-'Alaq). Ibn 'Abbas said: Had he called his retinue, the angels of punishment would have seized him at that very moment."
"694","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) was praying, and when he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn jumped on his back. When they wanted to prevent them, he gestured to them to leave them. When he finished the prayer, he placed them in his lap and said: ""Whoever loves me should love these two."
"695","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) was praying standing (voluntarily, and the door was in the qiblah), (locked). I sought to open the door, so he walked on his right or his left, opened the door, then returned to his place."
"696","[AI-translation] From Qabus from his father who said: My father sent a woman to 'A'isha to ask her: Which prayer was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) to persistently observe? She said: He used to pray four before Dhuhr, lengthening the standing in them and beautifying the bowing and prostration in them. As for what he would not leave whether healthy, sick, absent, or present, it was two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"697","[AI-translation] Sa'ib who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to pray before Dhuhr - after the sun's decline - four [rak'ahs], and he would say: ""The gates of heaven are opened (in it), and I love to present in it a righteous deed."
"698","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to pray between Maghrib and 'Isha'."
"699","Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh narrated from his father, who said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), how he used to pray. She said: He would pray Al-Hajir (the midday prayer), then pray two rak'ahs after it, then pray Al-Asr, then pray two rak'ahs after it. I said: But Umar used to strike people for them and forbid them? She said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray them himself, and he knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to pray them. But your people, the people of Yemen, are a people of Tugam (ignorant/foolish); they would pray Zuhr, then pray what is between Zuhr and Asr, then pray Asr, then pray what is between Asr and Maghrib. So Umar struck them, and he did well."
"700","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to pray while Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn played and sat on his back. The Muslims would try to lift them away, but when he turned (to leave), he said: ""Leave them - may my father and mother be sacrificed for them. Whoever loves me, let him love these two."
"701","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to teach us, saying: ""Do not precede the Imam (in bowing and prostrating). When he says Takbir, you say Takbir; and when he says: {Nor of those who went astray}, say Amin (for if his saying coincides with that of the angels, he will be forgiven) (his past sins). When he bows, bow; and when he says: 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah', say: 'Allahumma Rabbana lakal-hamd' (and do not raise before him); and when he prostrates, prostrate."
"702","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to recite in the two Rak'ahs of Fajr (and the two Rak'ahs after Maghrib) ""Qul ya ayyuhal-kafirun"" (Say: O disbelievers) and ""Qul huwa Allahu ahad"" (Say: He is Allah, the One)."
"703","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to recite in the Zuhr and Asr prayers ""Sabbih isma rabbikal-a'la"" (Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High) and ""Hal ataka hadithul-ghashiyah"" (Has there reached you the report of the Overwhelming)."
"704","[AI-translation] Mughira bin Shu'bah: He said, ""Al-Mughira bin Shu'bah dictated to me in a letter to Mu'awiyah that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say at the end of every obligatory prayer (when he gave Salam): 'La ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa ala kulli shay'in qadir. Allahumma la mani'a lima a'tayta wa la mu'tiya lima mana'ta wa la yanfa'u dhal-jaddi minkal-jadd.'"
"705","[AI-translation] Narrated Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him): The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to stand and pray during the night (on his Khumrah). (Maimunah said) And I was sleeping beside him (lying near the prayer mat of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)). When he prostrated, (the edge of) his garment would touch me while I was menstruating."
"706","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to sleep while prostrating, and his sleep could only be recognized by his breathing. Then he would stand and continue in his prayer."
"707","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to perform the Witr with one Rak'ah, and he used to speak between the two Rak'ahs and the (one) Rak'ah."
"708","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not perform the Tasbih (supererogatory prayer) during travel before it nor after it. Meaning: the obligatory prayer."
"709","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah: She used to scrape the semen off the garment of the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was praying."
"710","[AI-translation] Himmani said: I saw Anas bin Malik wearing a red fur, and he said: ""Our wraps during the era of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, we used to wear them and pray in them."
"711","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib: They used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, so when he bowed, they bowed. And when he said, ""Allah hears him who praises Him,"" they remained standing until they saw him placing his face (in another wording: his forehead) on the ground, then they would follow him."
"712","[AI-translation] From Suhayb from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Whenever they were frightened, they would resort to prayer."" Meaning: the prophets."
"713","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: When we were with the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, on a journey and we said, ""Has the sun passed the meridian or not?"" he would pray Dhuhr and then depart."
"714","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah bin Qura from his father who said: We were forbidden to stand in rows between the pillars during the era of the Messenger of Allah, and we were driven away from them strictly."
"715","[AI-translation] From Abdullah who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, was asked about Laylat al-Qadr, so he said: ""I was informed of it, but then it escaped me. So seek it in the last seven, or the last three."
"716","[AI-translation] From Aisha, elevated to the Prophet: ""For a woman to pray in her house is better than her praying in her chamber, and for her to pray in her chamber is better than her praying in the courtyard, and for her to pray in the courtyard is better than her praying in the mosque."
"717","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""For one of you to hold his hand back from the pebbles (in prayer) is better for him than a hundred camels, all black-eyed. And if Satan overcomes one of you, let him wipe just once."
"718","[AI-translation] From Aisha who said: We used to pray the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, wrapped in our cloaks, and we would depart while none of us could recognize the faces of others."
"719","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, elevated to the Prophet: ""Let a man pray in the mosque nearest to him, and let him not follow the mosques."
"720","[AI-translation] Hakam ibn Mina' that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar and Abu Hurayrah narrated to him that they heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say upon the planks of his pulpit: ""People must certainly stop abandoning their Friday prayers, or Allah will surely seal their hearts, and they will then be among the heedless."
"721","[AI-translation] From Jabir, mawquf: I do not like to greet the man while he is praying, and if he were to greet me, I would return the greeting to him."
"722","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, was asked about the time of the morning prayer. So he prayed when the dawn broke, then prayed again after it had brightened. Then he said: ""Where is the one who asked about the time of the morning prayer? What is between these two is a time."
"723","Abu Qatadah narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on a journey. He said: ""If you do not reach water tomorrow, you will suffer thirst."" So the swift ones among the people hurried off seeking water, but I stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). The Prophet's mount leaned to one side, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) dozed off. I propped him up, and he straightened. Then he leaned again, and I propped him up, and he straightened. Then he leaned until he almost fell off his mount, so I propped him up, and he woke up. He said: ""Who is the man?"" I said: ""Abu Qatadah."" He said: ""Since when have you been traveling?"" I said: ""Since last night."" He said: ""May Allah protect you as you protected His Messenger."" Then he said: ""Shall we camp?"" So he leaned toward a tree and dismounted. He said: ""Look, do you see anyone?"" I said: ""This is a rider, these are two riders,"" until they reached seven. We said: ""Guard our prayer for"
"724","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was praying at the end of the night. So I prayed behind him. He took me by the hand, pulled me, and made me stand beside him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned to his prayer, I stepped back. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prayed, and when he finished, he said to me: ""What is the matter with you?"" (In another narration: ""What is wrong with you?"") ""I place you beside me and you step back?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, is it appropriate for anyone to pray beside you while you are the Messenger of Allah whom Allah has given?"" He said: ""So he was pleased with me and supplicated to Allah for me to increase me in knowledge and understanding."" Ahmad added: ""Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sleep until I heard him breathing heavily, then Bilal came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! The prayer.' So he stood up and prayed without renewing his ablution."""
"725","[AI-translation] Zubayr, marfu': ""There is no obligatory prayer except that there are two rak'ahs before it."
"726","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes the prayer, and fasts Ramadan, it is a right upon Allah to admit him into Paradise, whether he strives in the cause of Allah or sits in the land in which he was born."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we not give glad tidings to the people?"" He said: ""Indeed in Paradise there are one hundred degrees which Allah has prepared for those who strive in His cause; the distance between each two degrees is like the distance between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest part of Paradise — and I think — above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it spring forth the rivers of Paradise."""
"727","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu': ""Whoever gives the adhan for twelve years, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and for his adhan each time, sixty good deeds are written for him, and for his iqamah, thirty good deeds."
"728","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatadah who said: My father entered upon me while I was bathing on Friday, and he said: ""Is this your bath for janabah or for Friday?"" I said: ""For janabah."" He said: ""Perform another bath, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Whoever bathes on Friday is in a state of purity until the next Friday.'"
"729","[AI-translation] Sanabihi: Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah led a people in prayer. When he stood for the prayer, he turned to his right and said: ""Are you pleased?"" They said: ""Yes."" Then he did the same to his left. Then he said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: 'Whoever leads a people in prayer while they are displeased with him, his prayer does not go beyond his collarbone.'"
"730","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise wider than it."
"731","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Whoever builds a mosque, not seeking thereby ostentation or fame, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"732","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: ""Whoever leaves the prayer while intoxicated once, it is as if he had the world and all that is in it and was stripped of it. And whoever leaves the prayer while intoxicated four times, it is a right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to make him drink from the mud of al-Khabal."" It was said: ""And what is the mud of al-Khabal, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""The exudate of the people of Hell."
"733","[AI-translation] From Yusuf bin 'Abdullah bin Salam who said: I came to Abu al-Darda in the illness in which he passed away, and he said to me: O son of my brother! What made you come to this town? Or what brought you? He said: I said: Nothing except maintaining the tie that was between you and my father 'Abdullah bin Salam. Abu al-Darda said: What an evil hour for lying this is. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then stands and prays two or four rak'ahs - Sahl doubted - perfecting in them the remembrance and humility, then seeks forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, he will be forgiven."
"734","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever observes these prescribed prayers is not written among the heedless, and whoever recites one hundred verses in a night is written among the devout."
"735","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Whoever fears he will not get up at the end of the night, let him perform Witr in the first part of it, and whoever hopes to get up at the end of it, let him perform Witr at the end of the night, for indeed the prayer at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."
"736","[AI-translation] Al-Sahihah number (2610), Sahih Muslim, Book of the Traveler's Prayer and its Shortening, Chapter on Whoever Fears He Will Not Get Up at the End of... Number (1255)"
"737","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever fills a gap, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise, and raise him by it a degree."
"738","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, who said: It is from the Sunnah when you enter the mosque to start with your right foot, and when you leave to start with your left foot."
"739","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) who said: It is from the Sunnah in prayer to place your buttocks on your heels between the two prostrations."
"740","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh bin Jabal, raised to the Prophet: Whoever fasts Ramadan, prays the prayers, and performs the pilgrimage to the House - I do not know if he mentioned Zakah or not - it is a right upon Allah to forgive him, whether he migrates in the cause of Allah or remains in the land where he was born. Mu'adh said: Shall I not inform the people of this? The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Leave the people (O Mu'adh) to act."
"741","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, raising it: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"742","[AI-translation] Qasri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is in the covenant of Allah, so let not Allah seek from you anything of His covenant, for whoever He seeks from His covenant for anything, He will catch him, then cast him on his face into the Hellfire."
"743","[AI-translation] From 'Aidh bin Qurt, marfu'an: Whoever prays a prayer and does not complete it, there is added to it from his glorifications until it is completed."
"744","[AI-translation] From 'Aidh bin Qurt who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever prays a prayer and does not complete it, there is added to it from his glorifications until it is completed."
"745","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, marfu'an: Whoever prays four (rak'ahs of) Duha and prays four before the first, a house is built for him in Paradise."
"746","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, said: Whoever prays the morning prayer in congregation, then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, then prays two rak'ahs, it will be for him like the reward of a complete Hajj and a complete Umrah, complete, complete, complete."
"747","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: Whoever prays for Allah for forty days in congregation, catching the first Takbir, two exemptions are written for him: exemption from the Fire and exemption from hypocrisy. It is narrated from the hadith of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, Abu Kahil, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him."
"748","[AI-translation] Aas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, that he said: Whoever stands (in prayer) with ten verses is not recorded among the heedless, and whoever stands with one hundred verses is recorded among the devout, and whoever reads one thousand verses is recorded among the muqantarin."
"749","[AI-translation] Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever reads Ayat Al-Kursi after every prayer, nothing stands between him and entering Paradise except death."
"750","[AI-translation] Dari that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, said: Whoever reads one hundred verses in a night, the qunut of a night is recorded for him."
"751","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever reads in a night one hundred verses is not recorded among the heedless, or is recorded among the devout."
"752","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Whoever does not pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr, let him pray them after the sun rises."
"753","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jābir, ascribed to the Prophet: A man is in prayer as long as he waits for it."
"754","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 754 Arabic Hadees:"
"755","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 755 Arabic Hadees:"
"756","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 756 Arabic Hadees:"
"757","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 757 Arabic Hadees:"
"758","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade Iqʿāʾ and Tawarruk in the prayer."
"759","[AI-translation] Narrated from ʿAlī: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade prayer after ʿAṣr except while the sun is elevated."
"760","[AI-translation] Anṣārī, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), that he said: Going out is obligatory upon every female wearing a wrapper. Meaning: for the two Eids."
"761","[AI-translation] Anṣārī, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), that he said: Going out is obligatory upon every female wearing a wrapper. Meaning: for the two Eids"
"762","[AI-translation] Naḥḥām of Banū ʿAdiyy b. Kaʿb who said: The call was made for Fajr on a cold day while I was in my wife's wrap. I said: I wish the caller would call out, ""And whoever remains seated, there is no blame on him."" So the caller of the Prophet (peace be upon him) called out: ""And whoever remains seated, there is no blame on him."
"763","Jabir ibn Abdullah reported: While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon, a caravan arrived in Medina, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rushed toward it until only twelve men remained with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you had continued to leave until not one of you remained, the valley would have flowed with fire for you."" Then this verse was revealed: ""And when they see merchandise or amusement, they disperse toward it and leave you standing"" (Al-Jumu'ah: 11). It is said that among the twelve who remained steadfast with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Abu Bakr and Umar."
"764","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abū Wāʾil who said: Ḥudhayfah said to ʿAbd Allāh (meaning Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him): (A group) is observing Iʿtikāf between your house and the house of Abū Mūsā, do not change it (in a narration: do not forbid them) while you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: There is no Iʿtikāf except in the three mosques. ʿAbd Allāh said: Perhaps you forgot and they remembered, or you erred and they were correct."
"765","[AI-translation] Juhanī, ascribed to the Prophet: Do not make your houses graves; pray in them."
"766","[AI-translation] Narrated from Sālim, from his father (ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar), ascribed to the Prophet: Do not take the mosques as thoroughfares except for remembrance or prayer."
"767","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), ascribed to the Prophet: Do not single out the night of Friday for standing (in prayer) from among the nights, and do not single out the day of Friday for fasting from among the days, unless it is a fast that one of you is observing."
"768","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, marfu': Do not pray towards a grave, and do not pray upon a grave."
"769","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Do not pray at the rising of the sun, nor at its setting; for it rises and sets between the horns of Satan. And pray whatever you wish in between that."
"770","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: There is no ghirar in prayer nor in tasleem. ( )"
"771","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Mas'ud: that he used to greet the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, with salam while he was praying, and he would return the salam to him. Then he greeted him with salam while he was praying, but he did not return it. Abdullah thought that this was due to some anger from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. So when he finished, he said: O Messenger of Allah! I used to greet you with salam while you were praying and you would return it to me. But I greeted you with salam and you did not return it to me, so I thought that was because you were angry with me. He said: No, but we were forbidden from speaking in the prayer except with the Quran and dhikr."
"772","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: None maintains the Duha prayer except an Awwab, and it is the prayer of the Awwabin."
"773","[AI-translation] From Said bin Nafi who said: Abu Bashir Al-Ansari, a companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saw me praying the Duha prayer when the sun had just risen. He disapproved of that and forbade me, then said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Do not pray until the sun rises high, for it rises between the horns of Satan."
"774","[AI-translation] Wadin bin Ata that Al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, saying: One of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, led us in prayer on the day of Eid, and he pronounced the takbir four, four. Then he turned his face towards us when he finished and said: Do not forget, like the takbir of the funeral. And he gestured with his fingers and clenched his thumb. Meaning in the Eid prayer."
"775","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr: that he held onto the ring of the door of the Ka'bah and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, except in Makkah, except in Makkah (except in Makkah)."
"776","[AI-translation] From Abu Qutaylah: that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, stood among the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: There is no prophet after me, and no ummah after you. So worship your Lord, establish your five, give your zakah, fast your month, and obey your rulers, [and] you will enter the Paradise of your Lord."
"777","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, ordered a man to lead the people in the Zuhr prayer, so he spat towards the Qiblah while leading the people in prayer. When the time for Asr prayer came, he sent for another man. The first man became afraid, so he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, has something been revealed concerning me? He said: No, but you spat in front of you while you were leading the people, so you annoyed Allah and His angels."
"778","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: No one hears the call (to prayer) in this mosque of mine and then leaves it -except for a need- and does not return, except a hypocrite."
"779","On the authority of Ibn al-Daylami, who used to reside in Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem), that he stayed in Medina seeking Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As. He asked about him and they said: ""He has traveled to Mecca."" So he followed him and found that he had gone to al-Ta'if, so he followed him there. He found him in a plantation walking side by side with a man from Quraysh, and the Qurayshi was carrying wine. When he met him, he greeted him with salam and he returned the greeting. He said: ""What brought you today? And from where have you come?"" So he informed him. Then he asked: ""Have you heard, O Abdullah ibn Amr, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) mention the drink of wine with anything?"" He said: ""Yes."" So the Qurayshi withdrew his hand and left. He said: ""I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: 'No man from my Ummah drinks wine but that his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings.'"""
"780","[AI-translation] Hanafi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his back between its bowing and prostration."
"781","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, raised to the Prophet: The Devil comes to one of you and pecks near his perineum, so he does not turn away until he hears a sound (or finds a smell)."
"782","[AI-translation] From Abu Fatimah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: O Abu Fatimah! Do much prostration, for there is no Muslim who prostrates to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, a prostration except that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, raises him by it a degree (in Paradise and erases by it a sin)."
"783","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to pray on a khumrah, and he said: O 'A'ishah! Put away this mat of yours from us, for I feared that it would tempt the people."
"784","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ turned away from the Fajr prayer and came to the women in the mosque and stood over them and said: ""O assembly of women, give charity, for I have not seen among those deficient in intellect and religion anyone who takes away the hearts of people of understanding more than you. And indeed I saw you as the majority of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. Draw near to Allah with whatever you are able."" And there was among the women the wife of Ibn Mas'ud... so she narrated the hadith: ""What is the deficiency of our religion and our intellects, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""As for what I mentioned of the deficiency of your religion, it is the menstruation that afflicts you; one of you remains for whatever Allah wills for her to remain, not praying. As for what I mentioned of the deficiency of your intellects, the testimony of a woman is half the testimony of a man."""
"785","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) who said: A caller is sent forth at the time of every prayer, and he says: ""O children of Adam, stand up and extinguish what you have kindled upon yourselves."" So they stand up and purify themselves, and their sins fall from their eyes, and they pray, and what is between them is forgiven. Then you kindle (sins) in between that, so when it is at the time of the first prayer, he calls: ""O children of Adam, stand up and extinguish what you have kindled upon yourselves."" So they stand up and purify themselves and pray, and what is between them is forgiven. Then when Asr prayer arrives, it is like that. Then when Maghrib prayer arrives, it is like that. Then when Isha prayer arrives, it is like that. So they sleep having been forgiven. Then he said: ""One who stays up late in goodness, and one who stays up late in evil."""
"786","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 786 Arabic Hadees:"
"787","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 787 Arabic Hadees:"
"788","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah b. 'Amir, raised to the Prophet: For every gesture a man makes (with his hand) in his prayer, ten good deeds are written; for every finger, a good deed."
"789","[AI-translation] Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: There will be a generation after sixty years. Then after them there will come a generation who squander the prayer and follow desires, so they will soon meet ruin. (Maryam) Then there will be a generation who recite the Quran but it does not pass their collarbones, and the Quran is recited by three: a believer, a hypocrite, and a wicked person."
